  "lei_pre_tch_tabela": "whole table struck through (repealed or replaced annex)",
  "lei_pre_tch_substituido": "struck through and followed by “Redação dada…”: it is the old wording",
  "lei_pre_tch_revogado": "struck through and marked as repealed",
  "lei_pre_tch_outro": "struck through in the original: old wording or repealed provision",
  "lei_pre_c_tachado": "Refusing keeps the struck passage in the text as ordinary text: the old wording shows next to the new and may become a “repeated article”; a repealed table enters as if it were in force.",
  "lei_pre_tch_identificador": "only the provision's number is struck through and the repeal note sits next to it: kept as it came (the note says it was repealed)",
  "lei_pre_tch_vazio": "(the whole line goes)",
  "lei_pre_ident_titulo": "Repealed identifiers kept ({n})",
  "lei_pre_ident_ajuda": "In these passages, only the provision's NUMBER is struck through (“Art. 217.”, “ANEXO XIV”, “§ 5º”…) — the “(Revogado pela…)” note sits next to it, without a strike: that is how the official site marks a repealed provision. Removing the number would erase WHICH provision was repealed (the article would vanish from the law, with no seal or warning) — so these never enter the decision list: they always stay as they came.",
  "lei_pre_ident_item": "line {l}: {t}",
  "lei_col_tch_ok": "Pasted with formatting: {n} struck passage(s) identified. You decide what to do with them in the review.",
  "lei_col_tch_nao": "The page has struck-through passages, but they could not be located in the pasted text. It was pasted as it came: the old text may show up next to the new.",
