  "lei_pre_g_remissao": "Lines that look like an article (or chapter) but are pieces of a sentence",
  "lei_pre_g_anexo": "Annexes (tables after the articles)",
  "lei_pre_h_invisiveis": "Soft hyphens, zero-width spaces and the like: they do not show, but they break text comparison.",
  "lei_pre_h_cabecalho": "Identical lines repeated at intervals through the text — each PDF page's header. They would sit in the middle of articles that cross a page and make identical articles look changed.",
  "lei_pre_h_pagina": "Lines that are only the page number (“Page 3 of 296”, or a 1, 2, 3… sequence).",
  "lei_pre_h_grafia": "“Art . 382” (space before the period), “Art. 356. A -” (which is article 356-A), quotation marks before “Art.” and “Parágra único”. Uncorrected, the reader does not split the article and its text sticks to the article above.",
  "lei_pre_h_remissao": "The PDF line break pushed a piece like “artigo 16 desta Lei” or “LIVRO II Regula…;” to the start of a line. The reader would take it for a new article (or chapter) and cut the real article in half. The suggestion is to join it to the line above.",
  "lei_pre_h_anexo": "Tables and charts at the end of the law. Without separating them, the whole annex becomes part of the last article.",
  "lei_pre_c_invisiveis": "If you refuse, the characters stay in the text.",
  "lei_pre_c_cabecalho": "If you refuse, the header stays inside the articles that cross a page, and they will look changed in an update.",
  "lei_pre_c_pagina": "If you refuse, the page number stays in the middle of the text.",
  "lei_pre_c_grafia": "If you refuse, the reader does not recognise that article: its text becomes part of the article above.",
  "lei_pre_c_remissao": "If you refuse, the reader creates a false article (or chapter) on that line and cuts the real article.",
