  "aj_titulo": "What the app adjusted while reading ({n})",
  "aj_expl": "When reading the law the app fixes a few details on its own, without touching the saved text. See what was adjusted and, if an adjustment is wrong, keep the original. It only changes how the law is read: the same button undoes it.",
  "aj_t_nota": "Amendment notes separated from the name ({n})",
  "aj_t_link": "Link words removed from the name ({n})",
  "aj_t_ordinal": "Article numbers read with “º” ({n})",
  "aj_t_sufixo": "Article numbers without the letter from the text ({n})",
  "aj_t_fora": "Lines left out of the reading ({n})",
  "aj_p_nota": "The copy brings a note such as “(Redação dada pela Emenda…)” next to the chapter name. The app separates the note from the name, to keep the name clean, and stores the note apart.",
  "aj_p_link": "In web copies the link “Regulamento” or “Vigência” comes glued to the end of the name. The app removes that word from the name.",
  "aj_p_sufixo": "“Art. 178 - A isenção…” is read as article 178, not 178-A: the “A” is the first word of the text. If it really is 178-A, keep the original.",
  "aj_p_ordinal": "“Art. 42O” (with the letter O) is read as “Art. 42º”: the copy replaced the º sign with the letter.",
  "aj_p_fora": "Lines that belong to no article (the start of the law, or what sits between a title and the first article) do not show in the reader. The saved text still has them. Nothing to decide here.",
  "aj_r_nota": "{r}: the note “{nota}” was separated from the name (“{nome}”)",
  "aj_r_nota_orig": "{r}: the note “{nota}” stayed with the name, as in the text",
  "aj_r_link": "{r}: “{link}” was removed from the end of the name (“{nome}”)",
  "aj_r_link_orig": "{r}: the name keeps “{link}” at the end, as in the text",
  "aj_r_ordinal": "Art. {de} read as Art. {para}",
  "aj_r_ordinal_orig": "Art. {de} read as it is in the text (not turned into “{para}”)",
  "aj_r_sufixo": "Art. {de} read as Art. {para}: the letter “{letra}” starts the text, it is not part of the number",
  "aj_r_sufixo_orig": "Art. {de} read as it is in the text (with the letter “{letra}” in the number)",
  "aj_r_fora": "{n} line(s) left out of the reading: “{antes}”",
  "aj_t_citacao": "Articles quoted from another law ({n})",
  "aj_p_citacao": "A law that amends another brings the new text in quotes, with the amending article and the amended one. Those quoted articles are NOT articles of this law: the app treats them as part of the amending article (and the paste cleanups leave them alone). If a block was read wrong, keep the original: the lines go back to being read as articles.",
