  "cq_bancada_disc": "Workbench",
  "cq_bancada_top": "Editor text",
  "pc_tipo_rico": "CARD TYPE: mix, as the content calls for, three types — (a) direct question (concept, deadline, competence); (b) True/False: front \"True or false: ...?\" and answer \"TRUE\" or \"FALSE — because ..., Art. X\"; (c) cloze with a hint, when the answer is a word or number the exam board swaps. A rule that often comes up as a trap becomes True/False. Do not use the same type for everything.",
  "pc_tipo_certo_errado": "CARD TYPE: ONLY True/False. Each card is a statement on the front — \"True or false: ...?\" — and the answer is \"TRUE\" or \"FALSE — because ...\", with the ground and the article. Make half true and half false; in the false ones, change ONE detail (deadline, subject, exception) and say which.",
  "pc_tipo_direta": "CARD TYPE: ONLY direct question (\"question :: answer\"), no cloze and no True/False. The answer carries the rule and its ground.",
  "pc_tipo_lacuna": "CARD TYPE: ONLY cloze ({{c1::term}}): the sentence from the source, with the term the exam board swaps hidden. One or two blanks per card, with a hint when there are two options ({{c1::30 days::30 or 60?}}). No question written inside a cloze card.",
  "pc_qtd_auto": "QUANTITY: whatever the content holds — one card per distinct idea of the summary, no fixed number. Do not pad cards to \"reach\" a quantity and do not repeat the same point.",
  "pc_qtd_n": "QUANTITY: at most {n} cards. If the content has fewer ideas, deliver fewer; never repeat the same point, nor paraphrase, to reach {n}.",
