  "ce_av_encolheu": "Block {n} came back SMALLER than the original and lost words. Check before accepting.",
  "ce_av_perdeu": "Block {n} lost content ({p}% of the original). Missing: {termos}.",
  "ce_av_continua": "Block {n} still lacks an essential requirement after the improvement.",
  "ce_prompt": "You will RAISE {n} existing memorisation cards to the standard of good exam decks. Do not change any card's subject: each stays on the SAME point, only more complete.\n\nWHAT TO DO ON EACH CARD (in this order of importance):\n1. The answer must explain itself, with at least 100 characters: the rule, the deadline, the exception and the why. Use ONLY what is in the card and in the SOURCE below.\n2. Every card ends with a \"+ Learn more — ...\" line (literal wording, example or outline). If \"+\" lines already exist, keep them.\n3. Cite the provision (\"Art. X, §Y\", precedent, law) when the source gives it. If the source does not, do NOT invent one: leave it out.\n4. Remove \"(Source: ...)\" from inside the question and the answer.\n5. A {{c1::...}} blank that mixes question and answer becomes a Basic card, or keeps at most 3 blanks and a dichotomous hint (\"A or B?\"). A Yes/No blank needs no hint.\n6. Keep the original tags.\n\nANSWER FORMAT: return each card under the SAME anchor \"@@ N\" (line on its own), in the app format: \"@ title\" above, \"question :: answer :: tags\" and the \"+\" lines GLUED right below (no blank line between, always \"+\", never \"*\", no repeated line). A card that has to be split may come back as several, all under the same anchor. Nothing before the first anchor or after the last card.\n\n{padrao_revisar}\n\nSOURCE:\n{fontes}\n\nCARDS:\n{trechos}",
  "cq_btn": "Repeated cards",
  "cq_btn_aj": "Looks across all topics for cards that ask the same thing in other words.",
  "cq_titulo": "Repeated cards",
  "cq_ajuda": "The app compares the questions of every card in your material and groups the ones that ask for the same point. For each group you choose which one stays; the others go to the trash (you can restore them). Nothing is deleted without your confirmation.",
  "cq_resumo": "{n} cards read · {g} groups of similar cards · {r} extra ({p}%)",
  "cq_sem_cartoes": "There are no cards saved in your material topics yet.",
  "cq_nenhum": "No groups of similar cards. Nothing to do here.",
  "cq_grupo": "{n} similar cards",
  "cq_mais_completo": "the most complete",
  "cq_manter_este": "keep only this one",
  "cq_mesclar": "merge into the most complete",
  "cq_mesclar_aj": "The card marked ★ stays. Whatever the others had extra (a different answer, an explanation) goes into its “learn more”, and the others go to the trash.",
  "cq_ignorar": "not a repeat",
  "cq_ignorar_aj": "This group stops showing up here. Nothing is deleted.",
  "cq_conf_manter": "Keep only this card?\n\n{f}\n\n{n} similar card(s) go to the trash (you can restore them).",
  "cq_conf_mesclar": "Merge into the most complete card?\n\n{f}\n\nWhat the other {n} knew extra goes into this one's “learn more”, and they go to the trash (you can restore them).",
  "cq_conf_tudo": "Resolve all {g} groups at once, merging each into its most complete card? {r} cards leave (the trash keeps the last 300; the “undo the last bulk resolution” button in this window brings everything back, and the workbench gets a version in History) and what they had extra is added to the card that stays. It may take a few seconds.",
  "cq_tudo_btn": "resolve all (merging)",
  "cq_mais": "show more groups",
  "cq_reexibir": "show the {n} hidden groups",
  "cq_feito": "{n} cards went to the trash and {m} “learn more” line(s) were merged.",
  "cq_erro_mesclar": "I could not find the card that stays in the saved text, so nothing was deleted.",
  "pc_tamanho": "SIZE AND DEPTH (numbers, not impressions):\n- Question up to {frente} characters.\n- Answer between {vmin} and {vmax} characters: the rule AND its ground (article, deadline, exception, consequence). A one-word or half-line answer is a weak card — complete it.\n- \"+\" lines (learn more): up to {mais} characters in total; put the literal wording, an example and the outline there.\n- If it does not fit, split into more than one card; never cut information.",
  "pc_qualidade": "QUALITY (the standard of good exam decks):\n- Whenever the source gives the provision, cite it in the answer (\"Art. 12, §2\") and put the literal wording on a \"+ Literal text — ...\" line. Only cite what is in the source; never invent an article.\n- A rule that often shows up as True/False: front \"True or false: ...?\" and answer \"TRUE\" or \"FALSE — because ..., Art. X\".\n- Cloze {{c1::...}}: at most 2 per card, each with a different number; when the choice is between two options, put the hint inside the blank: {{c1::answer::A or B?}}.\n- Only write \"★ Appeared in exam ▸ BOARD/YEAR\" (on a \"+\" line) if that information was given.\n- An \"@ Law > Topic > Subtopic\" line above the card says where the subject lives.\n- Never write \"(Source: ...)\" inside the question or the answer.",
  "pc_preservar": "DO NOT LOSE CONTENT:\n- Never summarise, cut or delete a number, deadline, article, exception or example from the original card.\n- A long card is SPLIT into new cards (allowed and expected); every fact of the original must reappear.\n- What you return, added up, must be equal to or larger than the original. Only remove literal repetition.",
  "pc_antidup": "DO NOT REPEAT: each fact becomes ONE card. Do not write the same point in other words (a paraphrase is a repeat), nor the same cloze with another blank.",
  "pc_antidup_lista": "DO NOT REPEAT: each fact becomes ONE card. Do not write the same point in other words (a paraphrase is a repeat), nor the same cloze with another blank. Cards with these questions already exist — do not generate another on the same point:\n{frentes}",
